 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return, defaults to no limit. When
+the header yields more ranges than `limit` (counting only valid ranges, after
+`combine` is applied), they are collapsed into a single range from the lowest
+start to the highest end, so some bytes between the original ranges may be
+included.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(200, 'bytes=50-60,0-10,100-120', { limit: 2 })
+// => [{ start: 0, end: 120 }]
+```
+
